error[SC0411]: `*box` is read before anything wrote it
   ╭─[ a_pointer_read_out_of_fresh_memory_on_the_right_of_a_comparison_is_reported.c:8:13 ]
   │
 8 │     int r = q == *box;
   │             ────┬────  
   │                 ╰────── read here
───╯
  = note: C17 7.22.3.1 p2 and 7.22.3.4 p2 leave what `aligned_alloc` and `malloc` allocate indeterminate until something writes it, and Annex J.2 lists using that value as undefined
  = note: this check belongs to safety level 1
  = help: write the slot before reading it, or allocate with `calloc`
